msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:21
msgid "\"outer::private\""
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:25
msgid "\"outer::public\""
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:30
msgid "\"outer::inner::private\""
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:34
msgid "\"outer::inner::public\""
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:48
msgid "Use the `pub` keyword to make modules public."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:50
msgid ""
"Additionally, there are advanced `pub(...)` specifiers to restrict the scope "
"of public visibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:53
msgid ""
"See the [Rust Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/visibility-and-"
"privacy.html#pubin-path-pubcrate-pubsuper-and-pubself)."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:55
msgid "Configuring `pub(crate)` visibility is a common pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:56
msgid "Less commonly, you can give visibility to a specific path."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/visibility.md:57
msgid ""
"In any case, visibility must be granted to an ancestor module (and all of "
"its descendants)."
msgstr ""
